## Rules

1. **`src/components/ui/`, `src/lib/utils.ts`, and `src/styles/globals.css`
   are template-managed.** Vendored from the shared Prop Firm Match brand
   tokens/components. Don't restyle inside them for a one-off need — add
   app-specific components elsewhere and compose with `Button`/`Card` from
   `src/components/ui/`. Editing these files directly will conflict the
   next time this repo runs `copier update`.
2. **To change a brand token or shared component for real**, the fix
   belongs in `pfm-app-template`, not here. Make the change there, then run
   `copier update` in this repo to pull it in as a reviewable diff — see
   below.
3. **Never hand-edit `.copier-answers.yml`**, except `_src_path` (if it ever
   needs pointing at a different remote/path) or `_commit` (only if
   `copier update` fails because the template's history was squashed/
   rewritten and the recorded commit no longer exists — see
   pfm-app-template's `MAINTAINING.md` Troubleshooting section) —
   everything else is copier's own record of the answers above and editing
   it breaks `copier update`.
4. Secrets: GitHub Secrets are CI-scope only (lint/test). Deploy-time
   secrets live in the Cloudflare dashboard (see `README.md` → Secrets) —
   don't add deploy credentials to GitHub Actions for this app.

## Pulling a template update

This repo has no `pfm-app-template` skill/plugin of its own — it's a
separate, already-generated repo. Don't assume that skill is loaded here;
follow the steps below directly.

0. **`copier` may not be installed.** Check with `copier --version` before
   anything else — don't ask the user to install it themselves first. If
   missing, install via `pipx install copier`, bootstrapping `pipx` itself
   if needed (same on macOS and Windows): find a working Python — try
   `python3 --version`, then `python --version` (Windows commonly only has
   `python`) — then run `<that-python> -m pip install --user pipx`
   followed by `<that-python> -m pipx ensurepath`. If neither resolves,
   Python itself is missing — tell the user, don't try to install a whole
   Python runtime yourself.
1. `git status` — must be clean, copier refuses to update a dirty tree.
   Commit or stash first if not; never discard uncommitted work to get
   there.
2. Confirm `.copier-answers.yml` exists at the repo root — if it's
   missing, this repo either wasn't generated from `pfm-app-template` or
   the file was deleted, and `copier update` has nothing to diff against.
3. Run:
   ```sh
   copier update --vcs-ref=HEAD --defaults
   ```
   `--vcs-ref=HEAD` is required, not cosmetic — this template has no
   release tags, and without it `copier update` looks for one and can
   behave unpredictably.
4. `git diff` — review before doing anything else. This diff is the entire
   point of using copier instead of a one-shot regenerate; don't skip
   straight to committing.
5. Show the user that diff and wait for their explicit go-ahead. Only run
   `git add -A && git commit` after they've actually approved it.

**If `copier update` fails**, don't guess at a fix — clone
`https://github.com/Prop-Firm-Match/pfm-app-template` (or fetch its
`MAINTAINING.md` directly) and read its Troubleshooting section, which
covers the specific failure modes already hit in practice (stale
`_src_path`, a squashed/rewritten template history orphaning `_commit`,
missing answers file, or — for an app generated a while ago — every auth/
data-source file showing as delete+add plus a whole-repo line-ending diff,
which is a real one-time transitional diff documented there, not a bug).
